Role in set: {{role}}.

COMPOSITION CATEGORY {{category}}: {{categoryRules}}
{{rules}}
Apply the ACTIVE RENDERING RULES above consistently. The set art contract refines these rules and must not contradict them.
INPUT REFERENCES: Transfer rendering from original art and category principles from matching-category art or diagrams. Do not copy objects, characters, UI or exact arrangements. Other-category art supplies rendering/material evidence only. Use the declared category for composition. When an attachment-role manifest is provided, follow each image’s take/ignore directions; original anchors define rendering, and supplemental examples cannot override them.
OUTPUT AND EXCLUSIONS: Render a single opaque PORTRAIT illustration with a width-to-height ratio of 43:48, matching the reference card format. No borders, text, watermarks, logos, unrelated extra objects or UI. People/characters are allowed only in category 5 as one or two characters performing a simple action. The ENTIRE subject, including wide brims, handles, cables and small protruding parts, must fit inside the central 80% of the image width and 86% of its height. Background artwork fills the canvas to every edge. Preserve the intended background as part of the image. The subject must remain clear at 430x480 and 107x120.
