GENERATION INPUT MANIFEST (1-based input order before transport packing): {{attachments}}
Input order is shuffled, not a ranking; references within the same declared role have equal authority. Follow each input purpose: original-rendering defines rendering/material treatment only; original-category also supplies composition principles for this category; supplemental is subordinate to originals; category-example demonstrates composition only; collection-example provides set context only. Never copy source subjects, screenshot chrome, diagrams or sheet layouts. Detailed take/ignore directions refine these roles without changing their authority.
REVISION CONTEXT: {{revision}}. If previousCandidate is present, use that numbered image as the edit base, change only the requested defect or smallest coherent correction, and preserve unaffected identity, geometry, viewpoint, placement, palette, lighting and background that comply with the accepted brief. Do not preserve a defect or treat the candidate as rendering authority. If absent, create a new image from the approved brief. Apply the shared art contract and all image-brief requirements even when specialist guidance is provided. Do not add text or watermarks. Typography is forbidden. People/characters are permitted only in category 5; categories 1–4 remain object-focused.
